course: dictionary
lesson: 6896
title: Overweight: two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Overweight has two meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. The first is about a living thing being heavier than is healthy for its height and age. «An overweight pet gets ill more often and lives a shorter life, so it needs fewer treats and more play.»
explain: The second meaning is about things being heavier than a rule allows. At the airport, an overweight bag costs extra because it is heavier than the limit. Ask yourself: is the word describing a body or a bag? That question tells you which meaning to use.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Overweight luggage» means heavier than the airline allows, and that fits. Being overweight in health lessons is usually linked to eating more than the body uses and not being active, so it is better to talk about healthy habits than to tease anyone.
fact: Overweight means heavier than is healthy for your height and age, or heavier than is allowed.
fact: Overweight is an adjective. It can describe a person, an animal or an object such as a bag.
fact: Useful phrases include «overweight luggage» and «slightly overweight».
fact: «A weight problem» usually means obesity, which is being very overweight.
fact: Being overweight can come from eating more than the body uses and not being active, so healthy habits help.
exercise: «An overweight pet gets ill more often.» What does overweight mean here? | Sleeping all day | Lighter than usual | *Heavier than is healthy for its size and age | Very hungry for treats
exercise: At the airport, an overweight bag costs extra. What does overweight mean for the bag? | Too small for the trip | *Heavier than the airline allows | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Priya says overweight means lazy. What is a better way to think about it? | *Overweight describes weight, and healthy habits help, so talking kindly about habits is better than teasing | Overweight means the same as underweight | Overweight means tall | Overweight means people should be teased
test: «The vet said the cat was slightly overweight.» What does slightly overweight suggest? | Exactly the right weight | Much taller than average | Very thin and weak | *A little heavier than is healthy
test: A bag can be overweight as well as a person. Which meaning fits the bag? | Happy and calm | Very old | Healthy for its size | *Heavier than allowed
exam: Which meaning fits «overweight luggage»? | Healthy and full of energy | *Heavier than the airline allows | Made of soft cloth | Very hungry
